WEBVTT

00:00.470 --> 00:02.020
- [Instructor] Averil was trying to factor

00:02.020 --> 00:05.270
six x squared minus 18x plus 12.

00:05.270 --> 00:08.550
She found that the greatest common factor

00:08.550 --> 00:13.240
of these terms was six
and made an area model.

00:13.240 --> 00:16.320
What is the width of Averil's area model?

00:16.320 --> 00:18.200
So pause this video and see
if you can figure that out,

00:18.200 --> 00:20.263
and then we'll work through this together.

00:21.120 --> 00:23.800
All right, so there's a couple
of ways to think about it.

00:23.800 --> 00:26.550
She's trying to factor six x squared

00:26.550 --> 00:29.160
minus 18x plus 12,

00:29.160 --> 00:32.230
and she figured out that the
greatest common factor was six.

00:32.230 --> 00:34.570
So one way you could think about it is

00:34.570 --> 00:39.250
this could be rewritten as
six times something else.

00:39.250 --> 00:40.690
And to help her think about it,

00:40.690 --> 00:42.320
she thought about an area model,

00:42.320 --> 00:45.320
where if you had a rectangle,

00:45.320 --> 00:47.520
if you had a rectangle like this,

00:47.520 --> 00:50.970
and if the height is six and the width,

00:50.970 --> 00:53.430
let's just call that the width for now,

00:53.430 --> 00:56.060
so this is the width right over here.

00:56.060 --> 00:58.440
If you multiply six times the width,

00:58.440 --> 01:00.800
maybe I could write width right over here,

01:00.800 --> 01:02.580
if you multiply six times the width,

01:02.580 --> 01:04.620
you multiply the height times the width,

01:04.620 --> 01:05.550
you're going to get the area.

01:05.550 --> 01:07.350
So imagine that the area of this rectangle

01:07.350 --> 01:08.920
was our original expression,

01:08.920 --> 01:12.920
six x squared minus 18x plus 12.

01:12.920 --> 01:15.230
And that's exactly what's drawn here.

01:15.230 --> 01:18.010
Now, what's interesting
is is that they broke up

01:18.010 --> 01:20.140
the area into three sections.

01:20.140 --> 01:24.080
This pink section is the six x squared,

01:24.080 --> 01:27.460
this blue section is the negative 18x,

01:27.460 --> 01:29.770
and this peach section is the 12.

01:29.770 --> 01:30.960
And, of course, these
aren't drawn to scale,

01:30.960 --> 01:33.270
'cause we don't even know
how wide each of these are

01:33.270 --> 01:34.500
'cause we don't know what x is.

01:34.500 --> 01:35.940
So this is all a little bit abstract,

01:35.940 --> 01:38.380
but it's to show that we
can break our bigger area

01:38.380 --> 01:40.340
into three smaller areas.

01:40.340 --> 01:43.230
And what's useful about
this is we could think about

01:43.230 --> 01:46.780
the width of each of these sub-areas,

01:46.780 --> 01:48.730
and then we can add them together

01:48.730 --> 01:50.300
to figure out the total width.

01:50.300 --> 01:54.120
So what is the width of this
pink section right over here?

01:54.120 --> 01:57.120
Well, six times what is six x squared?

01:57.120 --> 02:00.170
Well, six times x
squared is six x squared,

02:00.170 --> 02:02.400
so the width here is x squared.

02:02.400 --> 02:05.780
Now, what about this blue area?

02:05.780 --> 02:08.180
A height of six times what width

02:08.180 --> 02:10.440
is equal to negative 18x?

02:10.440 --> 02:13.560
So let's see, if I take
six times negative three,

02:13.560 --> 02:15.140
I get negative 18,

02:15.140 --> 02:17.710
then I have to multiply
it times an x as well

02:17.710 --> 02:18.990
to get negative 18x.

02:18.990 --> 02:22.950
So six times negative
three x is negative 18x.

02:22.950 --> 02:25.040
And then, last but not least,

02:25.040 --> 02:26.670
six, our height of six,

02:26.670 --> 02:29.090
times what is going to be equal to 12?

02:29.090 --> 02:31.690
Well, six times two is equal to 12.

02:31.690 --> 02:34.960
So we figured out the widths
of each of these subregions,

02:34.960 --> 02:36.840
and now we know what the total width is.

02:36.840 --> 02:39.550
The total width is going
to be our x squared

02:39.550 --> 02:43.420
plus our negative three x, plus our two.

02:43.420 --> 02:46.420
So the width is going to be x squared,

02:46.420 --> 02:47.580
and I can just write that as,

02:47.580 --> 02:51.430
minus three x, plus two.

02:51.430 --> 02:53.870
So we have answered the question.

02:53.870 --> 02:56.080
And you could substitute
that back in for this,

02:56.080 --> 02:57.880
and you could see, if
you multiplied six times

02:57.880 --> 02:59.760
all of this, if you distributed the six,

02:59.760 --> 03:03.573
you would indeed get six x
squared minus 18x plus 12.
